From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:59:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Buffered tui Kanban block notices re-read a stale
 ask at delivery

The legacy tui_gateway poller renders a notice when it claims it and holds it in
_kanban_pending behind a busy turn. PR #1260 refreshed a stale "Next action for the
user" ask only on the gateway admission path, so a buffered notice for a card that
finished meanwhile still asked the user to decide (review N3, t_01a1ce7ed2addb09).

kanban_claim_custody.batch_text joins the batch with each text passed through
refresh_stale_ask; the persisted kanban_notice row and the submitted turn use the same
text. The _KanbanText objects are not replaced, so claim identity and _kb_* attributes
stay intact. Still-blocked, remote and unreadable cards stay byte-identical.
